.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments - Payment lifecycle operations


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the full RAIL0 payment lifecycle.

.PP
Every on-chain operation is atomic: pass --private-key (-p) and the CLI prepares
the unsigned transaction, signs it locally, and broadcasts it in a single step.

.PP
rail0 payments authorize  -p @merchant-key --wait

.PP
Add -w/--wait to any of them to block until the chain confirms the operation,
rather than returning as soon as it is broadcast. A key is given as a raw 0x
hex key, as @name for one saved with 'rail0 keys add', or omitted to be
prompted for (hidden).

.PP
Authorize-and-capture flow — the buyer signs off-chain, the merchant submits:
  1. payments create -F @buyer -T @merchant -p @buyer-key   — buyer creates + signs
  2. payments authorize  -p @merchant-key -w       — merchant escrows
  3. payments capture    -a  -p @merchant-key -w  — merchant takes it

.PP
Charge (one-shot) flow — no escrow, funds move straight through:
  1. payments create -C -F @buyer -T @merchant -p @buyer-key
  2. payments charge  -p @merchant-key -w


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for payments


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


